# Auth Bootstrap — VTC Apps

JWT claim reference: `auth-jwt-reference.mdc`. Canonical lib exports: `lib-canonical.mdc`.

## URL injection (VTC shell opens child app)

**Personal** (`group=0`) — storage rules: `personal-storage.mdc`.

```
https://{appshortname}.apps.vtc.com/?token=...&user=29457&group=0&mode=light&color=%23004A80&lang=en&tz=America/Sao_Paulo
```

**Space** (example — shell injects space accent as `color`):

```
https://{appshortname}.apps.vtc.com/?token=...&user=29457&group=1205&mode=dark&color=%237C3AED&lang=en&tz=America/Sao_Paulo
```

| Param | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `token` | JWT for this session |
| `user` | User ID — must match JWT `user_id` after decode |
| `group` / `g` | `0` = personal; non-zero = active space `group_id` (same value) |
| `mode`, `color`, `lang` | Theme/i18n — `color` resolves runtime accent (`ui.mdc`) |
| `tz` | User IANA timezone from shell Settings → General — display times (`ui.mdc`); persist as `posif_tz` |
| `typography`, `font` | Network branding — `platform` \| `network` + `system` \| `lato` (`network-branding.mdc`) |

Child apps cannot read `app.vtc.com` localStorage. Bootstrap from URL `token` + `posif_token` in app localStorage.

**Shell chrome:** The platform iframe shows the app title (space display name) above the child app. Child apps **must not duplicate** that title in their sticky header — `ui.mdc` **Platform shell chrome**.

## Child app bootstrap (required)

On mount in `LayoutContent` or root client layout:

1. Read `token`, `user`, `group` from `window.location.search`
2. If `token` present: `localStorage.setItem('posif_token', token)`; optionally `posif_user`, `posif_group`
3. Call `preserveThemeParams()` on mount **before** stripping `token` from the URL — saves `mode`, `color`, `lang`, `tz`, `typography`, `font` to localStorage (`posif_*`)
4. Resolve accent in layout: URL `color` → `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ACCENT` → `getPersistedThemeParams().color` — `ui.mdc`
5. Resolve typography: URL `typography` / `font` → `applyAppTypographyToDocument()` — `network-branding.mdc`
5b. Resolve timezone: URL `tz` → `posif_tz` → browser — `resolveUserTimeZone()` from `@vtc/client` ≥ 1.2.2; format user-visible datetimes with that zone (`ui.mdc`)
6. If no URL token: `localStorage.getItem('posif_token')`
7. If still no token but valid `group` or `g` (non-zero): public guest browse (`public-guest-browse.mdc`) — **not** the promotional landing
8. If still no token and no `group`/`g`: show promotional landing page (`landing-page.mdc`) — Next.js `page.tsx` **and** static Vite `App.tsx`. Never an in-app OTP/login or a missing-token error.

All client `router.push` / internal links must use `addTokenToUrl()` so `color`, `mode`, `lang`, `tz`, `typography`, `font`, and tenancy survive navigation.

## Client helpers (`src/lib/clientAuth.ts`)

```typescript
const TOKEN_KEY = 'posif_token'
const MODE_KEY = 'posif_mode'
const COLOR_KEY = 'posif_color'
const LANG_KEY = 'posif_lang'
const TZ_KEY = 'posif_tz'

export function bootstrapAuthFromUrl(): void {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return
  const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search)
  const token = params.get('token')
  if (token) localStorage.setItem(TOKEN_KEY, token)
  const user = params.get('user')
  const group = params.get('group') ?? params.get('g')
  if (user) localStorage.setItem('posif_user', user)
  if (group) localStorage.setItem('posif_group', group)
}

/** Persist shell-injected theme params so accent survives token strip and client navigation. */
export function preserveThemeParams(): void {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return
  const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search)
  const mode = params.get('mode')
  const color = params.get('color')
  const lang = params.get('lang')
  const tz = params.get('tz')
  if (mode) localStorage.setItem(MODE_KEY, mode)
  if (color) localStorage.setItem(COLOR_KEY, color)
  if (lang) localStorage.setItem(LANG_KEY, lang)
  if (tz) localStorage.setItem(TZ_KEY, tz)
}

export function getPersistedThemeParams(): {
  mode?: string
  color?: string
  lang?: string
  tz?: string
} {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return {}
  return {
    mode: localStorage.getItem(MODE_KEY) ?? undefined,
    color: localStorage.getItem(COLOR_KEY) ?? undefined,
    lang: localStorage.getItem(LANG_KEY) ?? undefined,
    tz: localStorage.getItem(TZ_KEY) ?? undefined,
  }
}

export function getAuthToken(): string | null {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return null
  return localStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY)
}

export function addTokenToUrl(url: string): string {
  const urlObj = url.startsWith('http')
    ? new URL(url)
    : new URL(url, typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.location.origin : 'http://localhost')

  const token = getAuthToken()
  if (token) urlObj.searchParams.set('token', token)

  const user = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? localStorage.getItem('posif_user') : null
  const group = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? localStorage.getItem('posif_group') : null
  if (user && !urlObj.searchParams.has('user')) urlObj.searchParams.set('user', user)
  if (group && !urlObj.searchParams.has('group')) urlObj.searchParams.set('group', group)

  const current =
    typeof window !== 'undefined' ? new URLSearchParams(window.location.search) : null
  const persisted = getPersistedThemeParams()

  const lang = current?.get('lang') ?? persisted.lang
  const mode = current?.get('mode') ?? persisted.mode
  const color = current?.get('color') ?? persisted.color
  const tz = current?.get('tz') ?? persisted.tz

  if (lang && !urlObj.searchParams.has('lang')) urlObj.searchParams.set('lang', lang)
  if (mode && !urlObj.searchParams.has('mode')) urlObj.searchParams.set('mode', mode)
  if (color && !urlObj.searchParams.has('color')) urlObj.searchParams.set('color', color)
  if (tz && !urlObj.searchParams.has('tz')) urlObj.searchParams.set('tz', tz)

  return url.startsWith('http')
    ? urlObj.toString()
    : urlObj.pathname + urlObj.search
}
```

Prefer **`@vtc/client` ≥ 1.2.2** (`preserveThemeParams`, `addTokenToUrl`, `resolveUserTimeZone`) over forking the snippet above.

### `LayoutContent.tsx` (theme + auth mount)

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  bootstrapAuthFromUrl()
  preserveThemeParams()
  // then strip token from URL if present (keep color/mode/lang/tz in URL or localStorage)
}, [])

const persisted = getPersistedThemeParams()
const color =
  searchParams.get('color') ??
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ACCENT ??
  persisted.color ??
  undefined
const mode = (searchParams.get('mode') ?? persisted.mode) === 'dark' ? 'dark' : 'light'
const lang = searchParams.get('lang') ?? persisted.lang ?? 'en'

return (
  <ThemeProvider mode={mode} color={color}>
    …
  </ThemeProvider>
)
```

Call `bootstrapAuthFromUrl()` and `preserveThemeParams()` once after mount (inside `mounted` guard). Reference implementation: `~/apps/lists`.

## Server auth

- `await getAuthenticatedUser(request)` reads `token` from the request (URL query / Bearer)
- It confirms the token with the VTC API (`GET /api/v1/auth/verify`, `@vtc/auth` with
  `{ requireVerified: true }`) and only then returns `AuthenticatedUser`; otherwise `null`.
  Never decode the token yourself on the server to decide access (`auth-jwt-reference.mdc`).
- Missing/invalid → `{ success: false, code: "AUTH_401", error: "..." }` status **401**
- Use `user.user_id` and `user.group_id` in queries — snake_case, not camelCase

## Roles (summary)

| `role_type` | Typical name | Helper |
|-------------|--------------|--------|
| `"1"` | Owner | `isOwner()` |
| `"2"` | Admin | `isAdmin()` |
| `"3"`+ | Member | — |

Per-resource ACL: `access-control.mdc`. Catalog visibility: shell only — not app code.
